out
deprecated/embeddings-gpu/out

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository is PUBLIC. Nothing that authenticates anything may be
# committed. These patterns are a safety net, not a licence to keep secrets in
# the working tree — the real home for them is ~/.config/cheese (mode 600),
# which is outside the repo entirely.
#
# Note the deliberate absence of a blanket `*.env`: config/ports.env is tracked
# and required, and shadowing it would be worse than the risk this catches.

# Generated env files. `cheese-env` in particular is what install-cheese.sh and
# `cheese update-env` produce — it holds the registry and database credentials.
cheese-env
cheese-env*.conf
cheese-env-file.conf
.env
.env.*
*.local.env

# Credential files written by the cheese CLI, if anyone points them at the repo.
aws-credentials.conf
license-agent.env
supabase.env
cheese_license_file.json

# Keys and certificates. The *.template files the installer copies are tracked
# and unaffected — these patterns only match real, generated material.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
